{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"resistanceDistance","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"from","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"source","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"to","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"target","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"tolerance","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" = 1e-10, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maxIterations","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"? = nil) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"NoConvergence","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols13NoConvergenceV","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"? ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BinaryInteger","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sz","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Conjugate gradients on the Laplacian grounded at ","type":"text"},{"code":"target","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", from 0, until the residual’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Euclidean norm is at most ","type":"text"},{"code":"tolerance","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (relative to the right-hand side, which has norm 1),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or, on a weight spread that puts that below rounding, until the true residual stops","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"improving. Jacobi preconditioned for 300 iterations, then by a modified incomplete Cholesky","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"factor in maximum-spanning-tree order. O((n + m) √κ) time; about 9 n words, and O(n + m) for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the factor when it is built.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"weight","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" gives the conductance of the edge at each position, read once per position (every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"position, also outside the component); a weight of 0 is no edge.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","name":"Precondition","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"source"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"target"},{"type":"text","text":" are vertices of the graph, every weight is finite and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"nonnegative, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tolerance > 0"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"maxIterations"},{"type":"text","text":", when given, is at least 1."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"style":"note","name":"Throws","type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"","type":"text"},{"code":"NoConvergence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" after ","type":"text"},{"code":"maxIterations","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conjugate-gradient iterations (one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"matrix–vector product each; 20,000 + 2n when nil), with that count and the residual’s norm","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"relative to the right-hand side’s. No input has reached the default limit in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"measurements.","type":"text"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/resistanceDistance(from:to:weight:tolerance:maxIterations:)-7tzs1"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"text":"The resistance distance between ","type":"text"},{"code":"source","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"target","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (Klein and Randić 1993): the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"effective resistance between them when each edge is a conductance (its weight; 1 without","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"weight:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), (e_s − e_t)ᵀ L⁺ (e_s − e_t). 0 when they are the same vertex, without reading","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a